==Enemy==
Le'Behemoth stands at a shorter range than [[Le'boin]] (380 < 400) but has an Omni Strike of -100~410. Although not much, his piercing range, combined with the lack of backswing on his attacks, allows him to push more easily than if he just had 410 range, and easily decimating meatshields that either perish or flinch when he hits. Apart from these and a much more resilient [[Shield]] that never regenerates, Le'Behemoth isn't terribly different from your average Le'boin variant. Untrue to his name, he is not a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy.

His Omni Strike gives him the same reach as [[Le'noir]]; he is just barely outranged by [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]].

==Strategy==
Tanky meatshields paired with [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] are effective against him, since most of his health comes from his Shield. Once that is out of the way, he can be easily countered by long-ranged crowd-controllers like [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Heavy]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]].

Due to his range, it is recommended to mostly use big and bulky units to damage him, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] or many [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] capable of outranging him.

