==Trivia==
*The pentagram on his head is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Sigil of Baphomet|Sigil of Baphomet]].
*Like [[Miz Devil]], Le'Behemoth's [[Shield]] is set to regenerate with 50%, but can't, as he only has one knockback.
*He, [[Sinner Snache]], [[Condemned Peng]], [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Wicked Face]] were added to the game files in [[Version 10.8 Update|Version 10.8]], but were unimplemented and used [[Doge]]'s stats and sprites as placeholders until [[Version 10.9 Update|Version 10.9]].
*Because his hitbox starts at his feet, his Shield ends up clipping into his tusks, and certain units with very low ranges end up stopping inside his trunk.
*Despite his name, he is not a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy. This is a [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]-specific discrepancy caused by poor localization: the Behemoth type's Japanese name is "Super Beast" (超獣 ''Chōjū''), which is distinct from the "Behemoth" part in his Japanese name.
**[[wikipedia:Behemoth|Behemoth]] is a beast from Judea-Christian texts that was made at the beginning of creation. He is sometimes depicted as an elephant, although he has also been depicted as a water ox or hippopotamus. This creature's name is most commonly transliterated as ベヒモス ''Behimosu'' or ベヒーモス ''Behīmosu'' in Japanese, but the enemy's name spells it as ベヒモッス ''Behimossu''.
*Le'Behemoth's photos are likely risqué.
**In the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], his photos are described as ムフフな ''mafufu na''. This is an adjectival form of マフフ ''mafufu'', which is an onomatopoeia for mischievous or conspicuous laughter, similar to "tee hee", but when used as an adjective, it generally has the connotations of something being so sexy so you can't help but laugh.
**In the Taiwanese version, his photos are described as 清涼 ''qīngliáng'', which means "cool/refreshing", but can also be a euphemism for "scantly clad", especially of women.

